# MAGIC # 04 · The Insurance Domain — one governed home 🏛️
# MAGIC
# MAGIC This is where it comes together for the business. A **Domain** in **Catalog ▸ Discover** is a business-area home
# MAGIC that groups your trusted assets and explains them in plain language. We'll:
# MAGIC 1. **Create the `AXA Insurance` domain**
# MAGIC 2. **Bulk-import the glossary** as **pages** (business terms with definitions & synonyms)
# MAGIC 3. **Tag every asset** — gold tables, metric views, the Genie Agent — **into the domain**
# MAGIC 4. **Publish** so the whole business can discover it
# MAGIC
# MAGIC > 🖱️ **This entire notebook is a UI walkthrough.** Domains & Pages are **Discover-UI features** (no SQL / REST
# MAGIC > API today — docs: `docs.databricks.com/uc-semantics/pages`). Under the hood a domain is backed by a
# MAGIC > **governed tag**, and *adding an asset to the domain = assigning that tag* — which is the one part you *could*
# MAGIC > script later. The screenshots for each step are in the workshop deck.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ✅ **A finished example already exists in this workspace** — open it as you follow along:
# MAGIC [Discover ▸ AXA Insurance](https://fevm-serverless-stable-xhky6g.cloud.databricks.com/search/discover?q=domain%3A%22AXA%20Insurance%22)

