# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## Step 1 — Create the domain (≈2 min) 🖱️
# MAGIC 1. Left nav ▸ **Discover** (`/search/discover`).
# MAGIC 2. Top-right **Create ▸ Create domain**.
# MAGIC 3. Fill the form:
# MAGIC    - **Source** = *New tag* (a domain is backed by a governed tag; the name must be **unique in the account**)
# MAGIC    - **Name** = `AXA Insurance`  ·  **Subtitle** = *AXA P&C — governed underwriting & claims analytics*
# MAGIC    - **Description** (business framing): *"The single, governed home for AXA's P&C analytics. Business users
# MAGIC      start here to find certified data, KPIs, and the Genie Agent for underwriting and claims."*
# MAGIC    - Optionally set **Technical** and **Business Contacts**.
# MAGIC 4. **Create**. The domain opens in **Draft**.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC > ⚠️ **Two gotchas we hit live:** (a) the governed-tag name is account-unique — "Insurance" was already taken,
# MAGIC > so we used **"AXA Insurance"**. (b) The **Name is read-only after creation** (it's bound to the tag) — to
# MAGIC > rename, remove the domain and recreate. The domain **ID** is in the URL (`?domainId=…`) — you'll need it in Step 2.

