# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## Step 2 — Bulk-import the glossary as Pages (≈5 min) 🖱️
# MAGIC A **Page** is a governed business term — a definition, business use, and synonyms — that grounds Genie's answers.
# MAGIC Rather than hand-type each, use **bulk import**:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC 1. In the domain, **Create ▸ Create page** (opens the page editor, scoped to `AXA Insurance`).
# MAGIC 2. In the **Genie Code** panel on the right, click **"Bulk import pages"**.
# MAGIC 3. Provide your source — **paste the glossary text**, **upload a file** (PDF/CSV), or **connect** Confluence /
# MAGIC    GitHub / Google Drive. Say *"create one page per term, with a Definition, Business use, and the synonyms I list."*
# MAGIC 4. It proposes all terms in a **review table** (Name · Description · Synonyms · Status) and flags natural
# MAGIC    overlaps (e.g. *Combined Ratio* references *Loss Ratio* — expected). Choose **Create all**.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC > ⚠️ **Gotcha we hit live:** the importer resolves the domain by name and may fail ("domain didn't resolve").
# MAGIC > If so, paste the **domain ID from the URL** and ask it to use that — it then creates every page.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC **The AXA P&C glossary we imported (8 pages):**
# MAGIC
# MAGIC | Term | Definition | Synonyms |
# MAGIC |------|------------|----------|
# MAGIC | **Loss Ratio** | Incurred losses ÷ earned premium; core measure of underwriting profitability | LR, loss cost ratio |
# MAGIC | **Combined Ratio** | Loss ratio + expense ratio; below 100% = underwriting profit | COR |
# MAGIC | **Incurred Loss** | Paid loss + case reserves, before recoveries; ultimate cost of a claim | ultimate loss, incurred |
# MAGIC | **Earned Premium** | Written premium recognised as the policy term elapses; loss-ratio denominator | EP, earned |
# MAGIC | **Loss Run** | Claim-level listing (paid, reserve, incurred, recovery) from the claims table | claims bordereau, loss listing |
# MAGIC | **Claim Frequency** | Claim count ÷ policy count; how often claims occur | — |
# MAGIC | **Claim Severity** | Incurred loss ÷ claim count; average cost per claim | average severity |
# MAGIC | **Case Reserve** | Estimated unpaid amount on the open portion of a claim | outstanding, OS reserve |
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Pages are created in **Draft** — review each and **Publish**. On a published page you can also add **Related
# MAGIC Assets** (e.g. link *Loss Ratio* to `mv_portfolio`) so the term and the math are one click apart.

