# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## Step 3 — Tag every asset into the domain (≈3 min) 🖱️
# MAGIC "Associating an asset to the domain" = **assigning the domain's governed tag** to it. From the domain page:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC 1. Click **Add to domain**.
# MAGIC 2. **Catalog** tab ▸ search **`insurance`** ▸ click to select:
# MAGIC    - Tables: **`claims`**, **`policies`**, **`customers`**, **`premiums`**
# MAGIC    - Metric views: **`mv_portfolio`**, **`mv_claims`**
# MAGIC 3. **Add to domain**. Each confirms: *"The tag AXA Insurance has been assigned to …"*.
# MAGIC 4. Add the **Genie Agent** too: **Add to domain ▸ Workspace** tab ▸ select your
# MAGIC    *Insurance Claims and Underwriting Analytics* agent.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC > Now the domain contains **data + KPIs + the agent** — the full path from raw claim to trustworthy answer,
# MAGIC > discoverable in one place.

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## Step 4 — Publish & hand over 🚀
# MAGIC 1. On the domain, click **Publish** — it leaves Draft and appears under **Discover ▸ Browse by domain** for
# MAGIC    the whole business.
# MAGIC 2. Publish each glossary **page** you've reviewed.
# MAGIC 3. Set **Business / Technical Contacts** so users know who owns it.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ### What a business user now experiences
# MAGIC ```
# MAGIC   Open Discover ▸ AXA Insurance
# MAGIC        ├─ reads the glossary page "Loss Ratio" (definition + synonyms + linked metric view)
# MAGIC        ├─ finds the certified tables & metric views, all in one home
# MAGIC        └─ asks the Genie Agent "What's our loss ratio by line of business?"
# MAGIC              → answered from mv_portfolio → ≈64.6% overall, correct by LOB
# MAGIC ```
